7592186045417] [17592186549949 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549949 #edb/ref 1069 "q-251017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549949 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549949 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\sum }_{m=2}^{5}\\frac{2m+1}{10}=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ac819b8-8252-5f38-81b6-27fb48d49f54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549949 #edb/ref 1074 "The sum takes integer values of $m$ from $2$ to $5.$ So, computing the terms for $m=2,3,4,5$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{m=2}^{5}\\frac{2m+1}{10} & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1}{10}+\\frac{2\\cdot 3+1}{10}+\\frac{2\\cdot 4+1}{10}+\\frac{2\\cdot 5+1}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{11}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+7+9+11}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 16}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549960 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549960 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549960 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549960 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}5\\cdot {2}^{n-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549960 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "470997c7-250a-5a72-adc9-b7b406031a9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549960 #edb/ref 1074 "The sum takes integer values of $n$ from $1$ to $3.$ So, computing the terms for $n=1,2,3$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}5\\cdot {2}^{n-1} & =(5\\cdot {2}^{1-1})+(5\\cdot {2}^{2-1})+(5\\cdot {2}^{3-1}) \\\\  & =(5\\cdot {2}^{0})+(5\\cdot {2}^{1})+(5\\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 1)+(5\\cdot 2)+(5\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =5+10+20 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550004 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550004 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66995" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550004 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550004 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $S=8+16+24+⋯+80+88$ in sigma notation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550004 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dd5db24a-0334-5fd9-a195-a6f3785eda3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550004 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the terms of the corresponding sequence\n\n$$\n8,\\,16,\\,24,\\,…,\\,80,\\,88.\n$$\n\n are multiples of $8,$ and since $88÷8=11,$ there are $11$ terms in total. \n\nTherefore, the $n$th term of the sequence has the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=8n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ ranges from $n=1$ to $n=11.$ Indeed: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =8(1)=8 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =8(2)=16 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =8(3)=24 \\\\  & \\,\\,⋮ \\\\ {a}_{10} & =8(10)=80 \\\\ {a}_{11} & =8(11)=88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S=8+16+24+⋯+80+88={\\sum }_{n=1}^{11}8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550032 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f9dc2e7-7f93-5620-ae72-7c9fa71554d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550032 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186549949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550096 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186550032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550096 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ba61d36f-7149-5d34-b5ba-7a9fcfac6d9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550096 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186550004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550121 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186550096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550121 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fffeb167-2231-519c-b231-4f453c6d3104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550121 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186549960 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
